1
00:00:09,180 --> 00:02:03,770
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:08,350
No living creature was harmed during filming
this series

3
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:12,330
Episode 81

4
00:02:12,560 --> 00:02:13,640
Osman.

5
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:19,640
Don't.

6
00:02:22,190 --> 00:02:25,030
So you don't want to die.

7
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,370
But

8
00:02:28,150 --> 00:02:29,810
In my tradition...

9
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:34,020
...we don't show mercy to the cruels.

10
00:02:55,370 --> 00:02:56,810
Run fast!

11
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,420
Bring me the weapon!

12
00:03:37,260 --> 00:03:38,280
My Bey!

13
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:40,420
Let's cut them down!

14
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:45,990
Alps!
Do not shed the blood of brothers!

15
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:47,400
you

16
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:03,480
My Bey, we try, but there is no
end of them!

17
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:20,560
I will not stop until they end then.

18
00:04:21,730 --> 00:04:24,950
Thank that they are falling off one by one.

19
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:33,320
The rest are making our work hard enough!

20
00:04:56,940 --> 00:04:58,200
My Bey!

21
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:28,560
Osman will surely catch who did
this and make them pay, mother.

22
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:33,900
He is busy with them right now.

23
00:05:36,530 --> 00:05:38,930
If Osman's plan goes as planned

24
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:41,880
He must have killed the Vizier by now.

25
00:05:43,770 --> 00:05:44,860
But

26
00:05:44,890 --> 00:05:48,430
If something goes wrong about
the cemetery plan...

27
00:05:48,990 --> 00:05:50,620
There will be a large number
of soldiers ready to strike them.

28
00:05:51,340 --> 00:05:53,490
Then we will go and support
Osman Bey.

29
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:55,450
We shall wait for the news.

30
00:05:59,470 --> 00:06:00,510
Mother.

31
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:01,930
Mother.

32
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:07,520
Mother, you are fine, Thank Allah.

33
00:06:12,650 --> 00:06:14,020
Thank Allah

34
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:16,990
Thank Allah

35
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,540
I'm fine

36
00:06:19,120 --> 00:06:20,590
Osman.

37
00:06:23,020 --> 00:06:25,400
Is there any news about Osman

38
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:27,950
We will receive news, Inshallah, mother.

39
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:35,440
Selcan Hatun, thanks be to God
You are fine

40
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:43,260
She's fine, she's fine.

41
00:06:43,630 --> 00:06:45,520
My mother is a strong lady

42
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:47,260
She is Selcan Hatun!

43
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:50,970
Good news will arrive soon,
Inshallah (if Allah permits)

44
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,600
Inshallah (if Allah permits).

45
00:07:31,810 --> 00:07:33,800
Let's finish them!

46
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:37,260
So that we can
take care of the Vizier!

47
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:40,120
My Bey, they must be the last soldiers
in Sogut.

48
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:47,020
This Osman will be up to something.

49
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:49,960
We must be careful.

50
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:54,820
You are going to
build a sheltered place in this room

51
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,920
A shelter behind walls

52
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,950
It must be absolutely complete.

53
00:10:00,110 --> 00:10:02,280
There will be no shortage.

54
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:04,880
Your order, Hadrat Vizier.

55
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,240
Cerkutay!

56
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:07,510
My Bey!

57
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:09,100
Tie them up!

58
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:10,390
Your order, my Bey!

59
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:13,660
-Your order, my Bey!
- Come on!

60
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,280
You fight well, Kosses.

61
00:12:06,450 --> 00:12:07,580
Look

62
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:09,750
There are guys better than me.

63
00:12:15,110 --> 00:12:16,580
Praise be!

64
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:18,540
You are with us now

65
00:12:18,970 --> 00:12:21,260
But if you come out as our enemy later...

66
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,750
You see what might happen.

67
00:12:28,820 --> 00:12:30,080
Eyvallah (sure).

68
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,280
Kutan, Seran!

69
00:12:35,780 --> 00:12:37,380
Valiants, come on
tie up these soldiers.

70
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:38,620
Your order, my Bey.

71
00:12:51,920 --> 00:12:54,590
Why don't you kill us, Osman Bey?

72
00:12:54,620 --> 00:12:58,820
I don't kill Turkish soldiers who think
they are fighting for their country

73
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,160
because of a traitor leader's command

74
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:06,110
My problem is with Vizier
who has deviated from the truth.

75
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:09,320
That Vizier betrays Sultan

76
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:11,990
You will see this too!

77
00:13:12,260 --> 00:13:13,100
But...

78
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:17,430
Your souls are safe with us now.

79
00:13:17,890 --> 00:13:19,780
You still need to keep calm meanwhile.

80
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:21,330
Eyvallah (okay) Osman Bey.

81
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:28,960
Be good!

82
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,060
Cerkutay!

83
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,340
We won't kill them but...

84
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:41,680
We can beat them a bit.

85
00:13:42,010 --> 00:13:44,110
We'll get out of here before dawn.

86
00:13:44,470 --> 00:13:46,350
But first...

87
00:13:46,940 --> 00:13:49,220
I will see Vizier Alam Shah.

88
00:13:51,500 --> 00:13:53,790
If we can't get out...

89
00:13:54,370 --> 00:13:56,120
You know what to do.

90
00:14:13,640 --> 00:14:14,450
My Bey!

91
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:17,630
Vizier is absent!

92
00:14:22,940 --> 00:14:24,630
What are you saying?

93
00:14:31,780 --> 00:14:33,780
Stay with the soldiers, Alps!

94
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:45,880
Vizier!

95
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,840
You ran away like a snake

96
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:08,440
He can't jump from here
while injured, can he?

97
00:15:08,760 --> 00:15:11,080
If he had jumped, we'd see his body now.

98
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:16,740
I know the wound my sword caused!

99
00:15:17,890 --> 00:15:20,410
Why didn't this guy die then?

100
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:23,070
Coward Vizier!

101
00:15:24,760 --> 00:15:26,730
He wore armor inside his clothes then!

102
00:15:27,130 --> 00:15:29,350
So he saw that coming, huh?

103
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,720
- Baysungur!
- My Bey!

104
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,100
Look around, see if there is any trace.

105
00:15:35,270 --> 00:15:36,100
Your order, My Bey!

106
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,040
Cerkutay!

107
00:15:37,040 --> 00:15:39,720
- My Bey.
- Search every inch! Hurry!

108
00:15:41,170 --> 00:15:42,430
Hurry!

109
00:15:45,330 --> 00:15:48,180
Inegol Castle

110
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,360
No mistakes.

111
00:15:51,890 --> 00:15:55,000
No mistakes this time.

112
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:58,390
None!

113
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,540
Did Lord ever sleep?

114
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:17,620
Sleeping, Julia?

115
00:16:21,490 --> 00:16:27,200
My castle was given to the shepherd Gunduz,
that old dog is telling me what to do...

116
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:29,230
I can't sleep under these circumstances!

117
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:31,670
If I was an idiot...

118
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:33,380
I could sleep.

119
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:37,120
Just maybe I could.

120
00:16:41,670 --> 00:16:44,530
I thought that your agreement
with Vizier would satisfy you.

121
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:50,390
Yes, when Vizier was forced
to agree with me.

122
00:16:51,410 --> 00:16:55,430
But all things changed with the coming of
Geyhatu, Julia.

123
00:16:57,890 --> 00:17:03,180
Even though their offer
seems like an opportunity...

124
00:17:04,579 --> 00:17:06,280
With that devil Geyhatu...

125
00:17:07,348 --> 00:17:09,470
...is involved...

126
00:17:12,050 --> 00:17:15,450
I must have a third eye
at the back of my head!

127
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:19,240
Otherwise, my back...

128
00:17:24,099 --> 00:17:28,369
My back will turn into
a stage for goals like this, Julia

129
00:17:35,250 --> 00:17:36,320
Geyhatu.

130
00:17:38,110 --> 00:17:40,480
You seem to know him well, Lord Nicola.

131
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,440
If I kill you all...

132
00:17:44,870 --> 00:17:46,610
All lands were left to Osman...

133
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:50,910
If I make him Bey of the Beys....

134
00:17:53,340 --> 00:17:56,480
Wouldn't it be great?
Tell me.

135
00:17:59,810 --> 00:18:01,180
Geyhatu!

136
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:06,470
If you go down
to the well with his rope...

137
00:18:12,670 --> 00:18:16,440
He'll strangle you with that rope.

138
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,180
We are ready for your orders, sir!

139
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:34,650
The sun is rising.

140
00:18:35,770 --> 00:18:38,820
Prepare your soldiers, Argos.

141
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:40,220
We'll depart.

142
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:41,900
Your order, sir!

143
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:43,800
Lord Nikola!

144
00:18:45,050 --> 00:18:46,200
No matter where you go...

145
00:18:47,170 --> 00:18:49,030
I'll be by your side, you should
know that.

146
00:20:11,570 --> 00:20:12,440
Osman!

147
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,460
I will destroy you, Osman

148
00:20:21,810 --> 00:20:23,080
Sogut

149
00:21:06,990 --> 00:21:08,410
Commander Geyhatu!

150
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:10,410
Vizier Alam Shah is in Osman's hand.

151
00:21:11,220 --> 00:21:12,220
Osman wounded him.

152
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:36,160
I will take your soul Osman!

153
00:21:38,150 --> 00:21:39,020
Alam Shah!

154
00:21:40,950 --> 00:21:42,920
I thought you were smart!

155
00:21:44,850 --> 00:21:48,210
You are so stupid that you
fall into the hands of Osman!

156
00:21:50,730 --> 00:21:52,010
We'll kill Osman here.

157
00:21:53,070 --> 00:21:55,090
Here in Sogut.

158
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:42,440
You are somewhere here, Vizier!

159
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,840
You are definitely somewhere here!

160
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:49,800
You are somewhere here!

161
00:22:52,030 --> 00:22:53,990
Well, what if
he really jumped off the balcony?

162
00:22:54,240 --> 00:22:56,080
Osman Bey says look for him in the inn,
there must be something he knows

163
00:22:56,610 --> 00:22:57,930
He thinks he's in the inn.

164
00:22:57,930 --> 00:23:00,950
He sent his Alps out for him.
That means he is not fully sure.

165
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:04,190
What is the harm
of hard work, Kosses?

166
00:23:04,390 --> 00:23:06,110
Let's find this dog, help me!

167
00:23:06,170 --> 00:23:07,570
Let's find him, let's do it.

168
00:23:07,570 --> 00:23:08,670
Come on.

169
00:23:11,990 --> 00:23:12,720
Turgut!

170
00:23:23,850 --> 00:23:25,160
Vizier Alam Shah!

171
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:28,800
You won't even die on your honor,
but run away like a rat

172
00:23:29,430 --> 00:23:30,980
Hide wherever you want!

173
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:32,660
I will find you and take you out!

174
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:35,000
Alps!

175
00:23:35,930 --> 00:23:37,300
Search everywhere in detai!

176
00:23:37,710 --> 00:23:39,520
He must have left a trail behind!

177
00:23:41,010 --> 00:23:42,040
My Bey!

178
00:23:43,590 --> 00:23:45,000
There is no trace outside, my Bey!

179
00:23:45,400 --> 00:23:46,640
But... Geyhatu...

180
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:49,600
Geryhatu
encircled outside the inn.

181
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:53,800
What are you talking about?

182
00:24:03,300 --> 00:24:04,170
Damn it!

183
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:12,480
What is Geyhatu doing here?

184
00:24:13,760 --> 00:24:15,000
This is not good Osman Bey.

185
00:24:16,410 --> 00:24:17,740
It's not good at all.

186
00:24:18,270 --> 00:24:20,050
He sent his soldiers to the cemetery.

187
00:24:24,350 --> 00:24:28,080
His only concern is to see Vizier here.

188
00:24:30,040 --> 00:24:30,820
Alps!

189
00:24:34,150 --> 00:24:36,110
Find that Vizier
and bring him to me right away!

190
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:37,760
Bring him so that...

191
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:42,370
I can lay his corpse in front of Geyhatu!

192
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:44,380
Come on!

193
00:24:45,270 --> 00:24:46,060
Your order, my Bey!

194
00:24:46,290 --> 00:24:47,230
Come on, Alps!

195
00:24:56,850 --> 00:24:57,850
Can I, my sheik?

196
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:00,620
My sheik.

197
00:25:01,460 --> 00:25:02,420
Soldiers of the Mongols, Sheik...

198
00:25:04,010 --> 00:25:05,500
Mongol soldiers are attacking
Sogut, my sheik.

199
00:25:07,590 --> 00:25:10,390
Will you allow us to arm ourselves
with swords, my sheik?

200
00:25:11,820 --> 00:25:14,820
We haven't been armed with a sword
in the khanqah until now.

201
00:25:15,470 --> 00:25:16,620
Now it's time.

202
00:25:59,680 --> 00:26:00,890
Osman is in the inn.

203
00:26:04,070 --> 00:26:05,930
The great Geyhatu will take him.

204
00:26:08,520 --> 00:26:11,230
Do not try to help Osman.

205
00:26:13,270 --> 00:26:14,410
Whoever helps him...

206
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:19,800
...they will die.

207
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:30,410
It is the truth that determines our life.

208
00:26:31,910 --> 00:26:35,870
Your words are of no importance,
not even an iota.

209
00:26:36,490 --> 00:26:39,530
The outskirts of your khanqah
besieged by the Mongol soldiers

210
00:26:39,930 --> 00:26:42,340
If someone wants to die now...

211
00:26:46,220 --> 00:26:47,180
they can peek outside.

212
00:27:02,800 --> 00:27:05,810
Apparently it was the Vizier
who brought Geyhatu to these lands

213
00:27:06,810 --> 00:27:08,860
We don't know what's really going on.

214
00:27:10,770 --> 00:27:11,780
As they came here...

215
00:27:12,220 --> 00:27:13,970
They are aware of the existence of Osman
in Sogut.

216
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:15,530
What do we do now?

217
00:27:15,870 --> 00:27:17,640
Do you think Osman killed Vizier?

218
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:19,850
There is no news about them at the moment.

219
00:27:20,760 --> 00:27:22,750
But the Mongols know they are in the inn.

220
00:27:23,970 --> 00:27:25,200
Bala Hatun.

221
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,160
I want to fight too.

222
00:27:28,730 --> 00:27:30,380
You stay with my mother, Zehra.

223
00:27:31,470 --> 00:27:33,020
Calm down, Bala.

224
00:27:33,380 --> 00:27:35,690
Being idle like this bothers me, Malhun!

225
00:27:36,100 --> 00:27:37,260
Enough!

226
00:27:37,520 --> 00:27:40,190
Osman, my sheikh,
their lives are all in danger!

227
00:27:40,320 --> 00:27:42,190
If we go now, we can't help them!

228
00:27:42,540 --> 00:27:43,680
Mongols are everywhere!

229
00:27:43,780 --> 00:27:45,910
We have to think of something else, Bala!

230
00:27:45,910 --> 00:27:48,050
You are right, Bala.
Waiting is so annoying.

231
00:27:49,630 --> 00:27:51,760
But you should think of your child first.

232
00:27:52,660 --> 00:27:53,570
Enough.

233
00:27:54,730 --> 00:27:57,440
Instead of giving birth to my child
under the shadow of the cruels...

234
00:27:57,450 --> 00:27:58,330
...I prefer death!

235
00:27:58,610 --> 00:27:59,740
Get out of my way.

236
00:28:14,320 --> 00:28:15,610
Prepare your swords.

237
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:18,480
But keep your hearts calm.

238
00:28:34,500 --> 00:28:34,960
My Bey.

239
00:28:36,020 --> 00:28:37,210
Geyhatu's aide is coming!

240
00:28:37,630 --> 00:28:39,200
He's coming armless.

241
00:28:45,260 --> 00:28:46,970
He obviously doesn't want war.

242
00:28:48,990 --> 00:28:52,170
He will vomit the poison that
falls from Gikhato's tongue.

243
00:28:54,500 --> 00:28:55,400
Let him come.

244
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:57,970
Let him come.

245
00:29:18,450 --> 00:29:19,390
Osman Bey.

246
00:29:21,040 --> 00:29:21,870
Talk.

247
00:29:23,370 --> 00:29:25,290
Commander Geyhatu wants you.

248
00:29:26,630 --> 00:29:29,450
He is waiting for you to talk to him.

249
00:29:56,570 --> 00:29:58,430
Geyhatu will not leave you alive,
Osman Bey.

250
00:29:59,700 --> 00:30:00,960
Do not go.

251
00:30:01,790 --> 00:30:02,720
Turgut is right.

252
00:30:03,970 --> 00:30:05,780
If we all get out of here together...

253
00:30:06,160 --> 00:30:07,330
...we might have a chance.

254
00:30:08,030 --> 00:30:09,350
But if you go alone...

255
00:30:10,150 --> 00:30:11,570
We can't protect you then.

256
00:30:11,990 --> 00:30:12,500
No.

257
00:30:14,340 --> 00:30:18,360
Since the soldiers of the Mongols did not
break the door and attack us until now...

258
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:20,710
Geyhatu knows that
Vizier is in our hands.

259
00:30:21,330 --> 00:30:23,430
He won't do anything because we have him.

260
00:30:25,050 --> 00:30:26,030
But...

261
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:27,720
Alps!

262
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:28,830
The inn is ours!

263
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:30,960
The property is ours!

264
00:30:31,570 --> 00:30:33,440
That Vizier won't get out of here!

265
00:30:34,340 --> 00:30:36,430
Until I come back from Geyhatu...

266
00:30:36,980 --> 00:30:39,130
...tou will spread his corpse here!

267
00:30:39,700 --> 00:30:41,170
Your order, my Bey!

268
00:30:42,150 --> 00:30:42,770
Osman Bey.

269
00:30:44,590 --> 00:30:46,160
Be careful just in case.

270
00:31:02,440 --> 00:31:04,740
I came all the way to
fight with you, my Bey!

271
00:31:06,470 --> 00:31:07,570
Let me join you.

272
00:31:08,420 --> 00:31:09,110
No

273
00:31:09,940 --> 00:31:11,480
I'm not going to fight.

274
00:31:13,100 --> 00:31:14,860
It's a duel of words.

275
00:31:16,180 --> 00:31:18,340
You search for the Vizier
with the alps.

276
00:31:20,030 --> 00:31:21,170
Your command, my Bey.

277
00:32:07,120 --> 00:32:08,210
Osman!

278
00:32:09,090 --> 00:32:12,090
Fear the end I will prepare for you!

279
00:32:13,150 --> 00:32:15,495
You will die begging!

280
00:32:24,630 --> 00:32:26,330
Vizier!

281
00:32:29,220 --> 00:32:32,370
Vizier!

282
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:11,080
Vizier!

283
00:33:27,060 --> 00:33:29,490
Vizier!

284
00:33:42,010 --> 00:33:43,610
Vizier!

285
00:33:47,190 --> 00:33:50,180
Vizier!

286
00:33:59,140 --> 00:34:01,690
Vizier is a coward!

287
00:34:05,719 --> 00:34:08,020
He must have built
himself a secret hideout.

288
00:34:08,500 --> 00:34:12,460
Whether it is in the wall or underground!
We will take him out of where he hides!

289
00:34:21,170 --> 00:34:26,170
I'll make you all go through hell,
every one of you!

290
00:34:45,179 --> 00:34:46,590
I will survive.

291
00:34:48,960 --> 00:34:50,429
I will not die.

292
00:35:15,640 --> 00:35:42,740
Blood, blood, blood!

293
00:35:53,380 --> 00:36:16,560
Blood, blood, blood!

294
00:36:29,850 --> 00:36:30,730
Osman.

295
00:36:33,820 --> 00:36:35,430
You are in my hands again.

296
00:36:36,580 --> 00:36:37,950
I'm on my own land.

297
00:36:40,040 --> 00:36:42,260
You are in Sogut.

298
00:36:42,790 --> 00:36:46,270
Your land's future is up to my sword.

299
00:36:47,280 --> 00:36:51,170
I am able to ruin your lands.

300
00:36:52,010 --> 00:36:53,530
I would not keep you as a captive.

301
00:36:53,530 --> 00:36:57,130
I would destroy the castle
and plunder the city!

302
00:36:57,710 --> 00:36:59,130
I would cut off your head!

303
00:37:01,500 --> 00:37:04,960
Of course,
this happens if you don't surrender.

304
00:37:10,240 --> 00:37:14,690
It is clear that your intention is not
making me give up.

305
00:37:18,400 --> 00:37:23,320
Your intention is to take Vizier
safe and sound.

306
00:37:25,590 --> 00:37:27,910
He serves your dreams.

307
00:37:31,380 --> 00:37:33,030
But...

308
00:37:35,580 --> 00:37:37,150
...about the Vizier...

309
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:42,580
I have no intention of killing him
right now.

310
00:37:45,440 --> 00:37:48,030
I want to kill him slowly.

311
00:37:50,750 --> 00:37:53,160
You will give me Vizier Alam Shah!

312
00:37:53,690 --> 00:37:56,160
You will surrender!
You have no other chance.

313
00:37:59,460 --> 00:38:03,800
We have always a chance.

314
00:38:06,050 --> 00:38:09,100
Everything has a solution.

315
00:38:10,190 --> 00:38:14,490
Goktug was talking like you when
I took him as a hostage.

316
00:38:16,490 --> 00:38:19,500
I cut his heart!

317
00:38:25,960 --> 00:38:28,870
We can't let Geyhatu's soldiers
to wander around us, my sheik!

318
00:38:30,040 --> 00:38:33,010
My sheik, we should fight
and get Osman Bey out of the inn.

319
00:38:35,660 --> 00:38:37,970
Geyhatu's soldier informed us just now.

320
00:38:39,450 --> 00:38:43,340
Osman Bey decided to talk to Geyhatu.

321
00:38:47,570 --> 00:38:49,210
What are we going to do now,
my Sheik?

322
00:38:50,590 --> 00:38:53,790
We'll stand in silence...

323
00:38:54,440 --> 00:38:57,280
...and waiting for Osman Bey's move.

324
00:39:00,330 --> 00:39:04,030
If required,
we kill those outside and get to the inn.

325
00:39:31,110 --> 00:39:32,400
Osman.

326
00:39:33,560 --> 00:39:35,090
We were dragged into an empty cemetery.

327
00:39:36,560 --> 00:39:37,980
There is no funeral!

328
00:39:40,380 --> 00:39:43,890
Vizier Alam Shah!
I'm afraid he may be hurt.

329
00:39:45,740 --> 00:39:48,850
You are right.
We have to find Vizier Alam shah at once.

330
00:39:49,070 --> 00:39:50,020
Hurry.

331
00:40:04,460 --> 00:40:08,330
Don't say my brother's name
without permission!

332
00:40:10,140 --> 00:40:12,900
I know the games you and the vizier play!

333
00:40:15,090 --> 00:40:18,810
You deceived my brother and
made me lose my throne!

334
00:40:20,100 --> 00:40:24,570
You arranged an attack on the Sultan
And you accused me of all this!

335
00:40:25,310 --> 00:40:28,420
You have caused the bloodshed
of so many innocents and valiants!

336
00:40:29,300 --> 00:40:33,790
You will be held accountable for all of this!

337
00:40:35,080 --> 00:40:36,530
But first...

338
00:40:37,960 --> 00:40:41,000
But, first that Vizier.

339
00:40:42,850 --> 00:40:45,640
And then your turn will come too.

340
00:40:46,640 --> 00:40:48,890
The rebel Bey of the border regions, Osman!

341
00:40:50,130 --> 00:40:53,270
His tongue is as sharp as his sword!

342
00:40:55,500 --> 00:40:59,020
You like peace.

343
00:41:03,650 --> 00:41:09,220
Do not cause bloodshed
Give me the Vizier and surrender.

344
00:41:12,180 --> 00:41:15,270
All of you will continue living.

345
00:41:16,390 --> 00:41:21,120
If you don't surrender,
I will burn Sogut down.

346
00:41:32,900 --> 00:41:34,000
Geyhatu.

347
00:41:35,710 --> 00:41:41,290
Surrendering to the cruels
is dishonorable for us.

348
00:41:55,200 --> 00:41:57,550
You never change, Osman.

349
00:41:58,960 --> 00:42:03,220
If I find you even after fifty years...

350
00:42:04,330 --> 00:42:08,070
you will be the same man
and have the same stubbornness!

351
00:42:09,310 --> 00:42:13,710
Not fifty years
even if a thousand years have passed...

352
00:42:14,810 --> 00:42:19,130
The Turkish will be the Turkish himself
And his blood is the same blood!

353
00:42:20,240 --> 00:42:23,060
Our determination will not vanish!

354
00:42:27,890 --> 00:42:31,890
Have you seen, brother?
He doesn't hide his words even from Geyhatu.

355
00:42:32,490 --> 00:42:37,580
- Praise be to my Bey!
- Praise be, my Bey.

356
00:42:43,870 --> 00:42:47,000
Yes, Bey is a braveheart.

357
00:42:47,270 --> 00:42:50,210
Boran Alp, we didn't notice you.

358
00:42:51,380 --> 00:42:54,430
Brothers, I am here or not,
what's the difference?

359
00:42:55,560 --> 00:42:59,830
Here is Osman Bey who is standing
on the field like a lion in the face of Geyhatu

360
00:43:02,910 --> 00:43:04,290
Praise be!

361
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:08,400
I wish all of Kayi alps were there.

362
00:43:13,940 --> 00:43:17,210
You want to die so badly.

363
00:43:20,290 --> 00:43:27,110
You will drag down your alps and people!

364
00:43:34,870 --> 00:43:37,690
You are crowded.

365
00:43:40,820 --> 00:43:42,660
We are Turks.

366
00:43:44,070 --> 00:43:49,720
None of my warriors will fall
before killing ten of your soldiers.

367
00:44:07,690 --> 00:44:16,630
Blood, blood, blood!

368
00:44:16,630 --> 00:44:18,140
Is that so?

369
00:44:18,140 --> 00:44:28,480
Blood, blood, blood!

370
00:44:28,480 --> 00:44:31,390
Brothers! My Bey is coming!

371
00:44:45,700 --> 00:44:50,060
Assuming that you are back safe and sound,
Geyhatu is really asking the Vizier.

372
00:44:50,130 --> 00:44:51,510
You were right.

373
00:44:53,310 --> 00:44:56,280
We will fight until our
last drop of blood!

374
00:44:57,630 --> 00:44:59,870
It's time for war!

375
00:45:00,210 --> 00:45:01,730
War is a feast for us, my Bey!

376
00:45:02,460 --> 00:45:04,840
Show us the target, let us strike!

377
00:45:05,350 --> 00:45:10,280
Oh the joy of our souls, my Bey!
I'll meet my brother Goktug and Bamsi Bey.

378
00:45:11,370 --> 00:45:13,500
Command us to die, my Bey!

379
00:45:14,010 --> 00:45:16,010
Command us to go out and fight, my Bey!

380
00:45:18,290 --> 00:45:20,670
Even if my religion
is not the same as yours...

381
00:45:21,510 --> 00:45:26,370
Fighting on the same side with
such honorable soldiers honors me as well.

382
00:45:26,920 --> 00:45:29,140
Let's go and fight Osman Bey!

383
00:45:29,410 --> 00:45:33,420
Eyvallah Kosses, Eyvallah (Thank you).

384
00:45:33,990 --> 00:45:40,590
My Bey, we searched everywhere
but there is no trace of the Vizier.

385
00:45:46,240 --> 00:45:48,190
He is somewhere here.

386
00:45:49,150 --> 00:45:50,530
He's wounded.

387
00:45:51,600 --> 00:45:55,990
If he does not come out,
he'll die in the hole he hides in.

388
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:07,240
Kayı's Alps have always managed to
get rid of the enemy.

389
00:46:08,140 --> 00:46:09,720
We always have!

390
00:46:12,540 --> 00:46:15,680
What are the alps of Osman Bey will do?

391
00:46:16,930 --> 00:46:20,080
Look, the Mongols are
beating the drums of war!

392
00:46:21,510 --> 00:46:24,850
Should Osman Bey's alps
stay idle...

393
00:46:24,850 --> 00:46:28,080
...while Osman Bey is in a
difficult position?

394
00:46:28,080 --> 00:46:31,270
Of course we won't stay idle!
We are with our Bey.

395
00:46:31,270 --> 00:46:34,070
Praise be to my brothers!

396
00:46:36,280 --> 00:46:41,070
Inform the alps of Kayi.

397
00:46:42,640 --> 00:46:44,350
Today is the day of shahada.

398
00:46:46,080 --> 00:46:47,920
- Come on!
- Eyvallah (okay).

399
00:47:04,680 --> 00:47:06,560
Today is the day of shahada.

400
00:47:19,210 --> 00:47:20,760
Allah Allah!

401
00:47:21,690 --> 00:47:25,560
My Lord, whoever trusts you,
do not leave them alone.

402
00:47:31,360 --> 00:47:34,550
My sheik, we won't leave
Osman Bey there.

403
00:47:38,570 --> 00:47:40,070
O Almighty.

404
00:47:42,170 --> 00:47:46,270
O Almighty.
Allah is Amlighty.

405
00:47:47,450 --> 00:47:48,990
He prevents whoever he wants...

406
00:47:50,380 --> 00:47:53,450
..protects and sends help.

407
00:47:53,450 --> 00:47:55,660
Help us my Creator!

408
00:47:56,300 --> 00:47:58,610
- Amin.
- Amin.

409
00:48:00,630 --> 00:48:02,043
They are raging my sheik!

410
00:48:02,250 --> 00:48:03,230
They want blood!

411
00:48:03,310 --> 00:48:05,070
Let's go and bleed them!

412
00:48:06,410 --> 00:48:11,890
We will not hold our swords back
from the cruels.

413
00:48:12,630 --> 00:48:15,550
We will not leave Osman Bey there!

414
00:48:15,890 --> 00:48:17,450
Can I come in?

415
00:48:21,610 --> 00:48:22,890
Mother.

416
00:48:28,790 --> 00:48:29,630
My sheik.

417
00:48:31,170 --> 00:48:34,930
My Osman will take care of himself.

418
00:48:34,930 --> 00:48:36,930
But his son Orhan..

419
00:48:37,790 --> 00:48:39,470
He is alone.

420
00:48:39,470 --> 00:48:42,190
We have to think about him first.

421
00:48:42,190 --> 00:48:47,690
Mongols might want to take Orhan
to corner Osman.

422
00:48:47,890 --> 00:48:49,150
Mother.

423
00:48:49,510 --> 00:48:51,150
You are making me worried!

424
00:48:52,430 --> 00:48:53,910
May Allah protect him!

425
00:48:53,910 --> 00:48:55,910
Also, Gündüz Bey is with him Mother.

426
00:48:57,790 --> 00:49:01,070
I no longer have confidence in Gündüz.

427
00:49:01,070 --> 00:49:04,390
His eyes are blind to the truth
and his ears are deaf.

428
00:49:04,790 --> 00:49:06,930
Also, he must be coming here when he hears

429
00:49:14,730 --> 00:49:16,090
You are right, my Bey.

430
00:49:16,550 --> 00:49:18,950
It's easy to abduct Orhan
while Gündüz Bey is in Sogut.

431
00:49:19,610 --> 00:49:22,110
We'll go and take Orhan with Aygül.

432
00:49:23,590 --> 00:49:26,040
We'll get him and
come back right away, mother.

433
00:49:27,610 --> 00:49:32,310
Akca Dervish, send two dervishes
with Malhun Hatun.

434
00:49:34,510 --> 00:49:38,530
It's hard for me to leave you here while
Mongol dogs are outside.

435
00:49:38,930 --> 00:49:40,290
Don't think about us.

436
00:49:40,290 --> 00:49:42,390
Orhan's life is priority.

437
00:49:42,390 --> 00:49:45,170
Come on, go get him at once!

438
00:49:45,470 --> 00:49:47,170
My Sheik.

439
00:49:47,470 --> 00:49:48,630
Go, daughter.

440
00:49:49,050 --> 00:49:49,910
Mother.

441
00:49:50,210 --> 00:49:51,910
May your path be open, my daughter.

442
00:49:54,050 --> 00:49:56,780
- May your fight be holy, my sheik.
- Go now, daughter.

443
00:50:01,470 --> 00:50:04,390
And now, it's our time.

444
00:50:04,490 --> 00:50:05,590
Come on.

445
00:50:12,730 --> 00:50:17,610
Oh Allah, protect my children
and the whole Kayi tribe

446
00:50:44,950 --> 00:50:48,930
We are ready to burn Sogut,
Commander Geyhatu.

447
00:51:02,470 --> 00:51:03,730
Attack!

448
00:51:03,730 --> 00:51:05,730
For bloodshed!

449
00:52:05,850 --> 00:52:07,010
Brothers!

450
00:52:07,610 --> 00:52:09,010
My valiants!

451
00:52:10,270 --> 00:52:11,810
May our conquest be blessed!

452
00:52:11,950 --> 00:52:13,470
Eyvallah my Bey!

453
00:52:13,590 --> 00:52:14,700
My Bey!

454
00:52:15,650 --> 00:52:16,610
Kayi Alps...

455
00:52:17,050 --> 00:52:19,220
They rain arrows on
the Mongol soldiers!

456
00:52:29,650 --> 00:52:31,330
Praise be!

457
00:52:33,050 --> 00:52:35,290
We are walking behind the Kayi Bey.

458
00:52:38,770 --> 00:52:41,490
Come on, all to work!

459
00:52:43,390 --> 00:52:44,570
Come on alps.

460
00:53:08,730 --> 00:53:09,810
Alps!

461
00:53:56,630 --> 00:53:58,430
Allah is the greatest!

462
00:54:18,470 --> 00:54:20,650
Allah is eternal!

463
00:54:21,430 --> 00:54:23,170
Allah is right!

464
00:56:43,930 --> 00:56:45,470
Allah is the greatest!

465
00:57:09,210 --> 00:57:10,730
Stop your soldiers, Geyhatu!

466
00:57:18,850 --> 00:57:21,410
Impudent Gunduz!

467
00:57:21,890 --> 00:57:23,410
You need your soldiers.

468
00:57:24,090 --> 00:57:25,270
And I need my brother.

469
00:57:26,330 --> 00:57:29,070
Stop, don't let any more blood shed.

470
00:57:31,090 --> 00:57:33,190
Osman said his word.

471
00:57:34,310 --> 00:57:35,930
We will fight.

472
00:57:36,990 --> 00:57:40,570
And I'll cut off his head!

473
00:57:40,930 --> 00:57:43,310
Geyhatu! Listen me!

474
00:57:43,450 --> 00:57:47,050
I am the ally of the Vizier of Seljuk State

475
00:57:47,810 --> 00:57:49,110
Trust me!

476
00:57:51,750 --> 00:57:54,370
I'll convince my brother.

477
00:57:57,810 --> 00:57:59,230
Soldiers!

478
00:57:59,730 --> 00:58:01,030
Stop!

479
00:58:33,190 --> 00:58:34,430
Hurry up, Gunduz!

480
00:58:35,270 --> 00:58:36,990
My patience is running out!

481
00:58:37,870 --> 00:58:39,930
Convince Osman.

482
00:58:39,930 --> 00:58:44,590
Otherwise, I will demolish Sogut
over your heads!

483
00:59:09,950 --> 00:59:10,930
Osman Bey!

484
00:59:36,370 --> 00:59:37,490
I am listening.

485
00:59:50,170 --> 00:59:51,530
Won't you surrender?

486
00:59:55,370 --> 00:59:57,360
Are you going to let everyone die?

487
00:59:58,070 --> 00:59:59,670
Martyrdom.

488
01:00:06,770 --> 01:00:09,190
Since when did martyrdom become death?

489
01:00:10,890 --> 01:00:13,770
But this happens because of
your stubbornness, my brother!

490
01:00:13,870 --> 01:00:14,710
No it's not.

491
01:00:16,150 --> 01:00:17,970
No it's not.

492
01:00:19,030 --> 01:00:24,090
Our heart is never satisfied to
be a slave to the Minister like you.

493
01:00:26,210 --> 01:00:27,190
Ask them!

494
01:00:30,970 --> 01:00:31,790
Ask them!

495
01:00:34,750 --> 01:00:36,430
Ask them, my brother!

496
01:00:49,090 --> 01:00:51,050
Did you get your answer now?

497
01:00:52,570 --> 01:00:54,210
Gündüz Bey.

498
01:00:59,090 --> 01:01:00,830
Who trapped us here?

499
01:01:02,330 --> 01:01:05,130
Who helped Vizier claim Sogut?

500
01:01:05,590 --> 01:01:07,210
Tell me!

501
01:01:09,710 --> 01:01:11,380
Well, what about my mother?

502
01:01:13,390 --> 01:01:15,270
What about my mother?

503
01:01:16,070 --> 01:01:17,730
You should pray that...

504
01:01:17,730 --> 01:01:21,070
...my mother is alive.

505
01:01:21,990 --> 01:01:24,370
If anything had happened to her...

506
01:01:24,650 --> 01:01:26,990
I would kill you with my hands.

507
01:01:30,670 --> 01:01:33,210
Banishing my wives from the tribe!

508
01:01:33,590 --> 01:01:35,810
Separating my son from his mother!

509
01:01:35,970 --> 01:01:38,610
What does this mean?
Tell me, what does it mean?

510
01:01:44,670 --> 01:01:45,610
Yes.

511
01:01:48,650 --> 01:01:51,720
This is the kind of thing that
a Bey like you would do

512
01:01:57,030 --> 01:01:58,390
Open your eyes.

513
01:02:00,050 --> 01:02:03,350
Open your eyes brother, open them!

514
01:02:07,250 --> 01:02:09,710
You were about to involve in
my mother's death!

515
01:02:12,510 --> 01:02:14,910
And now you stand in front of me!

516
01:02:15,910 --> 01:02:17,390
And you tell me to surrender!

517
01:02:18,930 --> 01:02:20,550
I care Alps!

518
01:02:21,790 --> 01:02:22,890
I care you!

519
01:02:22,890 --> 01:02:25,120
You say you care me,
yet you burn my heart!

520
01:02:25,120 --> 01:02:27,610
You say you care the tribe,
yet you burn the tribe!

521
01:02:31,890 --> 01:02:37,290
Brother, Vizier blinded your eyes...

522
01:02:40,130 --> 01:02:42,578
deafen your ears.

523
01:02:54,790 --> 01:02:56,270
Vizier is in my hands.

524
01:03:00,930 --> 01:03:03,250
I will kill him slowly.

525
01:03:06,070 --> 01:03:07,170
Don't do it brother.

526
01:03:10,150 --> 01:03:11,710
Don't destroy us.

527
01:03:12,610 --> 01:03:13,710
Notice the reality!

528
01:03:13,710 --> 01:03:16,020
The reality is in front of you
and you ignore it!

529
01:03:16,020 --> 01:03:18,470
The reality calls for you to notice it!
You don't hear!

530
01:03:18,550 --> 01:03:20,570
Go get judged by Konya.

531
01:03:22,070 --> 01:03:24,130
Acquit yourself from those accusations.

532
01:03:26,050 --> 01:03:29,270
Games and hatred surrounded that justice.

533
01:03:32,870 --> 01:03:34,010
Only sentence...

534
01:03:36,504 --> 01:03:38,123
...is my sword!

535
01:03:45,540 --> 01:03:48,530
Bilecik Castle

536
01:03:48,590 --> 01:03:52,350
We will have such important
guests today, right...

537
01:03:52,350 --> 01:03:53,680
...my dear friend?

538
01:03:54,700 --> 01:03:57,370
Bilecik's chefs had already
started to work.

539
01:03:57,500 --> 01:04:01,090
They will prepare us a magnificent table.

540
01:04:01,470 --> 01:04:04,140
What table, what guest, Nikola?

541
01:04:04,720 --> 01:04:06,890
Besides, you still haven't given
me an answer.

542
01:04:07,580 --> 01:04:09,140
Why are we in Bilecik?

543
01:04:10,050 --> 01:04:12,440
Is it true what happened to Lord
Rogatus?

544
01:04:12,440 --> 01:04:13,980
Rogatus!

545
01:04:14,540 --> 01:04:16,900
He is paying the price for his betrayal.

546
01:04:16,900 --> 01:04:18,500
That's all.

547
01:04:19,140 --> 01:04:21,950
I heard the Seljuk Vizier
took over the castle.

548
01:04:23,550 --> 01:04:27,830
You should've asked the Vizier before
calling the other Lords here.

549
01:04:36,070 --> 01:04:38,500
His turn will come too.

550
01:04:39,250 --> 01:04:41,200
Don't worry.

551
01:04:41,640 --> 01:04:43,890
His turn will come too.

552
01:04:45,360 --> 01:04:46,600
But first...

553
01:04:46,740 --> 01:04:53,510
...I have a greatly advantageous offer for
you and the other lords, my dear friend.

554
01:04:56,140 --> 01:04:57,560
I don't know.

555
01:04:59,960 --> 01:05:01,820
I listened to you and came here.

556
01:05:02,650 --> 01:05:03,830
No, Nikola.

557
01:05:03,870 --> 01:05:05,420
I won't be at this dinner.

558
01:05:16,360 --> 01:05:18,000
My dear friend...

559
01:05:19,400 --> 01:05:20,930
... the truth is...

560
01:05:26,190 --> 01:05:29,040
...the main dish of this dinner's
menu is...

561
01:05:29,600 --> 01:05:32,340
...the lands.

562
01:05:33,560 --> 01:05:38,330
But if you keep insisting
that you will leave...

563
01:05:41,540 --> 01:05:49,160
...you'll be deprived of the main dish.

564
01:05:55,520 --> 01:05:56,420
You said well.

565
01:05:57,320 --> 01:05:59,020
You said well, my brother.

566
01:05:59,180 --> 01:06:01,940
You hit my mistakes one
by one in my face.

567
01:06:02,320 --> 01:06:03,670
Thank you.

568
01:06:05,090 --> 01:06:06,920
Now you face me as if...

569
01:06:07,280 --> 01:06:09,120
...you had done nothing, Osman.

570
01:06:10,310 --> 01:06:12,250
What Vizier said were slanders...

571
01:06:12,790 --> 01:06:13,940
...fine.

572
01:06:15,830 --> 01:06:18,070
Why did you escape from them, then?

573
01:06:19,600 --> 01:06:21,320
You threw our tribe into a fire!

574
01:06:21,800 --> 01:06:24,000
You tell me that I exiled the hatuns.

575
01:06:25,400 --> 01:06:28,030
Who provoked them and set them on me?

576
01:06:29,500 --> 01:06:31,780
You tell me that I stole the throne.

577
01:06:32,170 --> 01:06:33,260
Right?

578
01:06:34,010 --> 01:06:36,460
Who left the throne, Osman Bey?

579
01:06:38,720 --> 01:06:40,880
If there is a fire in Kayı...

580
01:06:41,550 --> 01:06:44,160
...you are the one who set it!

581
01:06:44,780 --> 01:06:46,980
How can one that is afraid of burning...

582
01:06:48,460 --> 01:06:50,580
... shine, brother?

583
01:06:54,820 --> 01:06:56,760
When did a Bey ever step back?

584
01:06:57,140 --> 01:06:59,510
Did my grandfather Süleyman Şah
ever step back?

585
01:07:00,130 --> 01:07:02,600
Did my father Ertuğrul Gazi
ever step back?

586
01:07:04,130 --> 01:07:05,820
The road was hard and...

587
01:07:06,190 --> 01:07:07,680
...you knew it, brother.

588
01:07:07,810 --> 01:07:09,420
You knew.

589
01:07:11,150 --> 01:07:13,690
Why did you let me down?

590
01:07:14,900 --> 01:07:15,880
Why?

591
01:07:16,390 --> 01:07:19,150
I didn't leave you or Kayı alone!

592
01:07:21,380 --> 01:07:23,950
Do you think I don't have
the same dream as you?

593
01:07:25,520 --> 01:07:27,230
For that dream, my brother...

594
01:07:29,060 --> 01:07:30,080
...surrender.

595
01:07:31,600 --> 01:07:34,920
Surrender so that the dream can come true.

596
01:07:34,980 --> 01:07:38,000
That dream doesn't come true by bowing
to the devil!

597
01:07:39,250 --> 01:07:42,740
They tried to kill the Sultan and blamed
it on me.

598
01:07:42,740 --> 01:07:45,580
I know you wouldn't try to kill
the Sultan, Osman!

599
01:07:45,580 --> 01:07:49,110
Then why are you on their side, brother?

600
01:07:49,130 --> 01:07:51,580
So that they won't ruin us, Osman!

601
01:07:52,220 --> 01:07:54,820
So that they won't destroy us, Osman!

602
01:07:58,320 --> 01:08:00,750
If one of us weren't on their side...

603
01:08:02,930 --> 01:08:04,600
...there would be no Kayı...

604
01:08:05,320 --> 01:08:06,750
...or no tribe, Osman.

605
01:08:09,350 --> 01:08:10,600
I had to.

606
01:08:14,229 --> 01:08:16,140
If you know everything...

607
01:08:19,170 --> 01:08:21,260
...then go tell Geyhatu that...

608
01:08:22,810 --> 01:08:24,740
...I will never surrender.

609
01:08:26,189 --> 01:08:28,779
Let him try his best!

610
01:08:39,720 --> 01:08:41,210
All right, brother.

611
01:08:55,670 --> 01:08:58,220
Brother!

612
01:09:10,010 --> 01:09:14,060
Master Geyhatu, Nikola gathered the lords.

613
01:09:14,060 --> 01:09:16,080
He is clearly up to something.

614
01:09:17,149 --> 01:09:21,479
Nikola is smart. He understood that I will
take his castle his lands.

615
01:09:21,479 --> 01:09:24,630
Take your men! He will be beheaded before
he returns to his castle!

616
01:09:31,500 --> 01:09:33,520
Are you all right, my Vizier?

617
01:09:33,720 --> 01:09:35,819
No one saw you, right?

618
01:09:36,050 --> 01:09:38,479
I didn't, don't worry.

619
01:09:39,359 --> 01:09:41,640
Geyhatu and his soldiers are outside.

620
01:09:42,140 --> 01:09:46,810
But neither Osman nor his alps are in
the tavern.

621
01:09:47,060 --> 01:09:48,920
Osman!

622
01:09:50,120 --> 01:09:53,899
Immediately inform Geyhatu that Osman is
not in the tavern.

623
01:09:53,899 --> 01:09:57,080
How could I leave you alone, my Vizier?

624
01:09:57,210 --> 01:09:58,200
You are wounded.

625
01:09:58,340 --> 01:10:00,980
Inform him at once, Celali.

626
01:10:01,190 --> 01:10:04,040
I am fine. I will get out of here
by myself.

627
01:10:24,520 --> 01:10:28,080
He doesn't listen, does he?

628
01:10:28,080 --> 01:10:29,520
He doesn't.

629
01:10:29,720 --> 01:10:31,950
Your brother is a rebel.

630
01:10:31,950 --> 01:10:34,820
He doesn't listen to his elder.

631
01:10:35,060 --> 01:10:38,010
I listen to Argun.

632
01:10:39,360 --> 01:10:45,780
Rebels like him are doomed to be crashed.

633
01:10:50,840 --> 01:10:54,040
Do you have anything to say?

634
01:10:54,430 --> 01:11:00,080
Are you going to protect Osman who tried
to kill the Sultan?

635
01:11:00,770 --> 01:11:01,780
Get out!

636
01:11:02,190 --> 01:11:03,180
Geyhatu!

637
01:11:04,110 --> 01:11:06,060
Let the siege continue.

638
01:11:06,680 --> 01:11:08,430
Hunger and thirst will surely...

639
01:11:08,920 --> 01:11:10,680
...make him surrender.

640
01:11:12,710 --> 01:11:14,340
Protect your soldiers.

641
01:11:14,540 --> 01:11:15,900
And I will protect my alps.

642
01:11:15,900 --> 01:11:18,660
It is done, Gündüz.

643
01:11:20,120 --> 01:11:25,980
Get out. Don't end up like Osman.

644
01:11:28,780 --> 01:11:29,960
Alps!

645
01:11:45,680 --> 01:11:47,960
Let me end up like my brother!

646
01:11:50,420 --> 01:11:54,860
I won't let one of you go without
killing me!

647
01:11:59,940 --> 01:12:02,940
Stop! Stop!

648
01:12:09,330 --> 01:12:10,490
Osman...

649
01:12:11,120 --> 01:12:14,310
...is not there. He escaped.

650
01:12:18,090 --> 01:12:20,590
Vizier Alemşah is alive.

651
01:12:24,940 --> 01:12:27,670
Find Osman!

652
01:12:28,010 --> 01:12:33,940
Burn the tavern down!
Burn the Söğüt down if necessary!

653
01:13:05,780 --> 01:13:07,060
Osman has escaped!

654
01:13:07,220 --> 01:13:08,480
Find him!

655
01:13:22,220 --> 01:13:23,570
Thankfully!

656
01:13:26,130 --> 01:13:27,680
Thankfully!

657
01:13:30,950 --> 01:13:33,680
Osman!
Osman!

658
01:13:33,820 --> 01:13:35,580
Osman!

659
01:13:36,780 --> 01:13:38,320
Osman!

660
01:13:41,820 --> 01:13:43,260
Search everywhere!

661
01:13:45,040 --> 01:13:46,820
Osman!

662
01:14:03,250 --> 01:14:04,840
Vizier Alemşah!

663
01:14:07,380 --> 01:14:09,180
Where did Osman escape?

664
01:14:12,310 --> 01:14:13,060
Soldiers

665
01:14:13,820 --> 01:14:15,840
Find me the way Osman used to escape!

666
01:14:17,450 --> 01:14:18,640
Osman!

667
01:14:29,840 --> 01:14:33,400
I am glad if Vizier Alemşah died.

668
01:14:33,870 --> 01:14:37,520
But if he is alive, we leave here now
so that...

669
01:14:38,140 --> 01:14:39,630
...we can kill him.

670
01:14:39,950 --> 01:14:41,410
He has no chance of surviving.

671
01:14:41,520 --> 01:14:43,460
He can't live with that wound for long.

672
01:14:46,260 --> 01:14:47,850
You did what's best, Osman Bey.

673
01:14:48,140 --> 01:14:49,850
Otherwise, everyone would get hurt.

674
01:14:51,940 --> 01:14:53,640
You saved Söğüt, my Bey.

675
01:14:55,860 --> 01:14:58,110
Also, we killed many tyrants, my Bey.

676
01:15:02,700 --> 01:15:05,220
If the oppressor persists in
his cruelty...

677
01:15:05,820 --> 01:15:07,060
...his end is near.

678
01:15:08,820 --> 01:15:11,980
Victory is near if the one on
the right path...

679
01:15:12,360 --> 01:15:13,470
...persists in the war

680
01:15:15,360 --> 01:15:19,670
Now we will live to be their executers.

681
01:15:24,080 --> 01:15:26,940
Come on! We are going to Çoban!

682
01:15:28,490 --> 01:15:29,440
Come on!

683
01:15:38,930 --> 01:15:39,870
Osman!

684
01:15:42,690 --> 01:15:45,010
Osman!
Osman!

685
01:15:48,480 --> 01:15:49,370
Osman!

686
01:15:51,450 --> 01:15:55,320
One of Osman's man's blood, Geyhatu.

687
01:15:56,240 --> 01:15:59,840
-They escaped from a secret passage.
-What are you waiting for?

688
01:16:00,540 --> 01:16:02,190
Find him, now!

689
01:16:02,680 --> 01:16:05,550
Find him!
Get out!

690
01:16:07,710 --> 01:16:08,630
I will go too.

691
01:16:09,710 --> 01:16:12,070
It is my duty to avenge Vizier Alemşah.

692
01:16:12,720 --> 01:16:16,070
Go. Get me Osman's head!

693
01:16:22,260 --> 01:16:23,630
Where are you going, Ferman?

694
01:16:24,430 --> 01:16:26,380
You must stay with Vizier Alemşah.

695
01:16:26,760 --> 01:16:28,920
Celali is enough for my Vizier.

696
01:16:29,570 --> 01:16:31,440
We need more soldiers to kill Osman.

697
01:17:13,640 --> 01:17:16,370
What is this, Master Davut?

698
01:17:17,590 --> 01:17:18,750
Master Davut...

699
01:17:19,910 --> 01:17:21,560
...it is clear that...

700
01:17:22,620 --> 01:17:24,480
...you do your duty properly.

701
01:17:25,240 --> 01:17:28,620
We are on the job, my Bey.

702
01:17:43,200 --> 01:17:44,670
Tell me, Master Davud...

703
01:17:46,450 --> 01:17:47,150
...tell me...

704
01:17:48,480 --> 01:17:50,290
...how many swords did you make?

705
01:17:51,860 --> 01:17:55,490
I made as many swords as
the lives of infidels...

706
01:17:55,900 --> 01:17:58,370
... that you took while you were away...

707
01:17:59,270 --> 01:18:00,710
...my Bey.

708
01:18:02,060 --> 01:18:04,160
Praise be!

709
01:18:04,330 --> 01:18:05,660
Great job.

710
01:18:05,850 --> 01:18:06,960
Thank you, my Bey.

711
01:18:09,420 --> 01:18:11,260
I guess I couldn't understand.

712
01:18:11,640 --> 01:18:14,230
Isn't the Söğüt under the control
of the Vizier?

713
01:18:15,800 --> 01:18:17,580
Do you think we let go...

714
01:18:18,450 --> 01:18:20,830
... every time we get into trouble,
Kosses?

715
01:18:22,510 --> 01:18:24,350
The swords aren't made in Söğüt.

716
01:18:26,790 --> 01:18:27,840
It is...

717
01:18:29,980 --> 01:18:31,630
...this love of conquest...

718
01:18:34,120 --> 01:18:35,930
...that keeps me alive...

719
01:18:39,010 --> 01:18:41,150
...in these difficult times.

720
01:18:47,260 --> 01:18:48,910
We spoke with Master Davut before.

721
01:18:49,940 --> 01:18:51,110
Until the heart stops...

722
01:18:52,220 --> 01:18:55,040
...forging hammers will never stop.

723
01:18:55,980 --> 01:18:57,020
Thank you.

724
01:19:01,330 --> 01:19:02,470
Thank you.

725
01:19:04,150 --> 01:19:05,520
You say nice but...

726
01:19:06,610 --> 01:19:09,680
...what if you weren't able to get out of
that tavern, Osman Bey?

727
01:19:10,180 --> 01:19:12,070
Then, it would be left to Orhan.

728
01:19:22,270 --> 01:19:23,480
Rogatus is here, my Bey.

729
01:19:32,310 --> 01:19:34,360
Osman Bey, Kosses!

730
01:19:35,820 --> 01:19:36,910
You are still alive!

731
01:19:37,010 --> 01:19:39,420
You too, my old friend!

732
01:19:41,340 --> 01:19:44,220
I brought you crucial news
from Constantinople.

733
01:19:45,210 --> 01:19:48,100
I can tell.

734
01:19:48,940 --> 01:19:50,380
Tell me, Rogatus.

735
01:19:50,810 --> 01:19:52,030
The Emperor is furious!

736
01:19:52,320 --> 01:19:54,160
He found out that Geyhatu came.

737
01:19:55,000 --> 01:19:57,490
He makes too much sound.

738
01:19:59,790 --> 01:20:01,840
He is mad that the lords are
looking for...

739
01:20:01,840 --> 01:20:05,300
... other things while there is
the Mongol danger.

740
01:20:08,750 --> 01:20:10,400
What is he planning to do?

741
01:20:10,800 --> 01:20:12,610
He will gather...

742
01:20:13,140 --> 01:20:14,680
...all his trusted commanders...

743
01:20:16,460 --> 01:20:17,760
...in the Sagoros' Castle.

744
01:20:18,460 --> 01:20:20,770
He will go there secretly.

745
01:20:26,680 --> 01:20:27,600
Good.

746
01:20:28,700 --> 01:20:29,420
Good.

747
01:20:31,580 --> 01:20:34,040
I hope the Emperor Andronikos...

748
01:20:35,090 --> 01:20:38,020
...he is tolerant of unexpected guests.

749
01:20:41,070 --> 01:20:42,720
Since, I will be there too.

750
01:20:44,560 --> 01:20:47,590
We need more soldiers to stand against
Geythatu.

751
01:20:49,700 --> 01:20:51,750
My troop has already arrived
at the castle.

752
01:20:51,850 --> 01:20:53,310
We will take them with us too.

753
01:20:53,920 --> 01:20:56,230
We are stronger together, Osman Bey.

754
01:20:57,790 --> 01:21:01,320
My alps are also always ready for war.

755
01:21:02,070 --> 01:21:05,610
But are these soldiers enough, Osman Bey?

756
01:21:17,730 --> 01:21:22,790
Let me give you good news!

757
01:21:25,060 --> 01:21:28,940
Do not let the native Montenegrins...

758
01:21:29,740 --> 01:21:32,650
...be destroyed!

759
01:21:34,580 --> 01:21:41,400
Don't let the rough tree be cut down!

760
01:21:44,160 --> 01:21:51,730
Don't let the splendid water
flowing like blood dry up!

761
01:21:53,950 --> 01:22:00,900
May your wings don't break!

762
01:22:03,450 --> 01:22:10,290
May fate not make you needy!

763
01:22:13,400 --> 01:22:18,260
Don't let your white-brown horse...

764
01:22:19,120 --> 01:22:23,390
...stumble while running!

765
01:22:25,200 --> 01:22:26,930
Praise be!

766
01:22:28,200 --> 01:22:29,200
Praise be!

767
01:22:31,280 --> 01:22:33,050
Praise be!

768
01:22:37,180 --> 01:22:38,430
Soon, my Orhan.

769
01:22:39,070 --> 01:22:39,800
Soon.

770
01:22:41,020 --> 01:22:43,920
It is soon that you meet your parents
again.

771
01:22:48,700 --> 01:22:52,710
If you keep quiet, my Orhan will meet
his parents, Ayşe Hatun.

772
01:22:53,280 --> 01:22:54,120
Malhun Hatun!

773
01:22:54,870 --> 01:22:55,900
How did you get in?

774
01:22:56,280 --> 01:22:57,550
I came to take my Orhan.

775
01:22:57,880 --> 01:22:59,470
I wish to take him easily.

776
01:23:00,090 --> 01:23:02,420
Come on, give me my son.

777
01:23:02,690 --> 01:23:04,300
He belongs to his mother.

778
01:23:04,580 --> 01:23:05,450
Don't I know.

779
01:23:06,070 --> 01:23:06,950
I am a mother.

780
01:23:07,880 --> 01:23:10,930
Also, Orhan missed his mother very much.

781
01:23:13,080 --> 01:23:14,880
Come on, take your son.

782
01:23:18,180 --> 01:23:19,840
My son!

783
01:23:27,110 --> 01:23:27,910
Aygül.

784
01:23:29,530 --> 01:23:30,670
Thankfully!

785
01:23:30,800 --> 01:23:33,150
Let's go.
The alps are changing guard.

786
01:23:33,650 --> 01:23:34,810
Be careful.

787
01:23:35,450 --> 01:23:36,450
I worry about you.

788
01:23:36,580 --> 01:23:38,050
Don't worry, Ayşe Hatun.

789
01:23:38,330 --> 01:23:40,500
Two alps are waiting for us outside.

790
01:23:40,880 --> 01:23:43,170
Let's go to Osman Bey, Aygül.

791
01:23:44,020 --> 01:23:44,800
Let's go.

792
01:23:45,140 --> 01:23:47,460
Let's reunite them.

793
01:23:48,040 --> 01:23:49,290
Wait.

794
01:23:52,550 --> 01:23:55,120
Cover him with this.

795
01:23:56,770 --> 01:23:58,410
May my Allah protect you.

796
01:23:59,690 --> 01:24:00,420
Come on.

797
01:24:02,070 --> 01:24:03,950
Come on.
Come on.

798
01:24:12,890 --> 01:24:15,250
I will wipe out Osman's lineage!

799
01:24:16,360 --> 01:24:17,300
Edebalı...

800
01:24:18,980 --> 01:24:21,480
...you will be punished!

801
01:24:22,250 --> 01:24:25,860
I will fill up the lodge with your blood!

802
01:24:26,000 --> 01:24:29,920
I will drown you in that blood!

803
01:24:30,340 --> 01:24:31,800
Calm down, Geyhatu!

804
01:24:33,200 --> 01:24:34,830
I will talk to Sheik Edebalı.

805
01:24:35,770 --> 01:24:38,350
It is no longer the time to talk, Gündüz!

806
01:24:38,510 --> 01:24:40,280
It is time for them to pay!

807
01:24:40,680 --> 01:24:42,150
I will burn Söğüt down!

808
01:24:42,510 --> 01:24:50,320
Geyhatu! I will call my soldiers anytime
I want!

809
01:24:52,730 --> 01:24:55,490
Leave the lodge and Söğüt alone!

810
01:24:57,670 --> 01:24:59,000
You need us!

811
01:24:59,150 --> 01:25:01,230
Am I stuck with your weak horse...

812
01:25:02,440 --> 01:25:05,490
...your unarmed soldier, Gündüz?

813
01:25:06,020 --> 01:25:09,670
Geyhatu, I have the strongest horses!

814
01:25:10,760 --> 01:25:14,170
I have the most valiant of the soldiers!

815
01:25:16,990 --> 01:25:20,110
Don't make a mistake by succumbing
to your anger.

816
01:25:22,460 --> 01:25:24,490
You need me.

817
01:25:24,490 --> 01:25:28,770
The more you talk the angrier I get!

818
01:25:30,460 --> 01:25:33,660
I don't want to talk anymore, Gündüz!

819
01:25:33,860 --> 01:25:39,970
You will join my army with a thousand
horses and a thousand soldiers.

820
01:25:44,160 --> 01:25:45,060
Get out!

821
01:25:53,850 --> 01:25:57,050
Watch the tribe and the lodge!

822
01:25:57,050 --> 01:26:00,250
Find Osman wherever he is!

823
01:26:00,750 --> 01:26:02,910
Sure, Master Geyhatu!

824
01:26:52,620 --> 01:26:54,320
Where is he!

825
01:26:56,070 --> 01:26:58,480
Find him!
Kill him!

826
01:27:35,690 --> 01:27:37,090
Soldiers!

827
01:27:46,160 --> 01:27:48,910
I never trusted you, Konur.

828
01:27:54,970 --> 01:27:57,220
I knew you would betray.

829
01:27:57,610 --> 01:27:59,310
You are just following the order.

830
01:28:00,250 --> 01:28:02,440
Get off your dagger or
I will have to hurt you.

831
01:28:04,750 --> 01:28:07,050
Vizier Alemşah loved you, Konur.

832
01:28:09,050 --> 01:28:10,720
He will be upset.

833
01:28:42,320 --> 01:28:45,290
Not everyone gets enough time to choose
the right side, Ferman.

834
01:28:49,330 --> 01:28:52,720
We are in this world to serve Allah
and surely we will return to Allah.

835
01:29:04,360 --> 01:29:06,920
Soldiers!
Retreat!

836
01:29:45,540 --> 01:29:46,950
Let's go find Osman!

837
01:29:48,950 --> 01:29:51,290
First, we need to find the tracks.

838
01:29:53,870 --> 01:29:54,990
Tracks.

839
01:30:01,420 --> 01:30:04,570
We have to find my Bey
before those dogs do.

840
01:30:10,500 --> 01:30:12,070
We shouldn't be seen together.

841
01:30:12,730 --> 01:30:14,470
What we are going to face is unclear.

842
01:30:15,900 --> 01:30:17,650
Eyvallah, you are right.

843
01:30:19,360 --> 01:30:22,000
Then let's get you dressed.

844
01:30:22,000 --> 01:30:24,250
Come with me, come on.

845
01:30:32,380 --> 01:30:36,450
Did Vizier teach you not asking for permission
before entering the khanqah, Gündüz Bey?

846
01:30:36,880 --> 01:30:37,870
Stop there!

847
01:30:38,120 --> 01:30:40,560
Are you still talking, Akca Dervish?

848
01:30:40,840 --> 01:30:44,920
You tested me with my mother's pain!

849
01:30:45,480 --> 01:30:47,200
You said she's dead!

850
01:30:47,790 --> 01:30:51,850
While the Mongols had been raiding
Sogut because of Osman's stubbornness, right?

851
01:30:52,490 --> 01:30:54,290
What do I have to tell you anymore?

852
01:30:54,820 --> 01:30:56,580
Don't say anything, Gündüz Bey.

853
01:30:59,900 --> 01:31:04,710
You haven't talked sanely for a long time.

854
01:31:07,750 --> 01:31:12,900
Do you know what I had to do
to protect you, my sheik?

855
01:31:14,280 --> 01:31:17,680
Geyhatu had taken an oath to
destroy the Khanqah.

856
01:31:20,510 --> 01:31:23,320
Do you know how difficult it was
to talk him out of it?

857
01:31:24,990 --> 01:31:28,610
Don't you see the situation that
you put me in, my sheik?

858
01:31:29,720 --> 01:31:36,500
I would prefer dying to
obeying the cruels!

859
01:31:37,870 --> 01:31:42,870
I wish you had joined
in our case of righteousness...

860
01:31:43,810 --> 01:31:47,950
But you trusted the fake
with the fear of losing your life.

861
01:31:56,240 --> 01:31:59,570
You may consider me as wrong.

862
01:32:01,330 --> 01:32:04,170
My Allah knows my attention.

863
01:32:07,940 --> 01:32:10,850
If you insist on not listening to me...

864
01:32:11,810 --> 01:32:15,240
I'll do things I don't want to.
Just for the sake of peace of Sogut.

865
01:32:21,050 --> 01:32:23,030
Can I, my sheik?

866
01:32:32,690 --> 01:32:34,910
What more are you going to do,
Gündüz Bey?

867
01:32:35,480 --> 01:32:37,590
Are you trying to go beyond yourself?

868
01:32:40,290 --> 01:32:42,530
Give me patience, my Allah!

869
01:32:44,440 --> 01:32:46,890
You won't do anything without
telling me anymore!

870
01:32:47,510 --> 01:32:49,490
Those things you do on your own...

871
01:32:53,390 --> 01:32:55,510
....throws the whole Sogut into the fire

872
01:32:55,510 --> 01:32:58,940
What kind of brother are you?
You don't see us, understand us!

873
01:32:59,780 --> 01:33:02,540
You are still accusing us.

874
01:33:05,080 --> 01:33:07,210
May my Creator show you mercy.

875
01:33:13,730 --> 01:33:14,690
Where is my mother?

876
01:33:15,510 --> 01:33:16,380
I will see her.

877
01:33:17,420 --> 01:33:19,130
Mother doesn't want to see you!

878
01:33:55,990 --> 01:33:59,390
Is Rogatos on our side just to
go to the Emperor?

879
01:34:01,470 --> 01:34:02,430
Tell me!

880
01:34:03,750 --> 01:34:05,080
Are you with us in the war?

881
01:34:13,060 --> 01:34:13,790
I...

882
01:34:15,060 --> 01:34:18,560
I don't really know what to think of
this union which is consisted of old enemies.

883
01:34:22,480 --> 01:34:23,590
I'm a Lord.

884
01:34:25,060 --> 01:34:27,370
I still have two loyal commanders.

885
01:34:29,810 --> 01:34:33,190
Two commanders means two
great troops.

886
01:34:34,560 --> 01:34:36,520
I will order them to join you.

887
01:34:39,500 --> 01:34:42,950
You realize how big this case is,
my friend Rogatus.

888
01:34:43,330 --> 01:34:44,780
Yes, we get it.

889
01:34:45,260 --> 01:34:49,280
What about your commanders?
Do they realise how big this is?

890
01:34:49,760 --> 01:34:54,670
They will fight for Turks for the first time,
not against them.

891
01:34:56,300 --> 01:35:00,310
You are talking about men who would
rather die than surrender to the Mongols.

892
01:35:03,880 --> 01:35:07,730
Uniting with Turks is not
worse than death.

893
01:35:10,340 --> 01:35:11,470
However...

894
01:35:13,560 --> 01:35:16,190
Guarantee their loyalty.

895
01:35:19,460 --> 01:35:23,070
I hold you responsible for
the simplest mistake they make

896
01:35:25,160 --> 01:35:26,390
There will be no error.

897
01:35:27,450 --> 01:35:30,870
We will gouge out the eyes of those who
set their sights on our lands.

898
01:35:31,580 --> 01:35:35,360
I hope we don't have a
conflict afterwards.

899
01:35:35,690 --> 01:35:37,360
Time will reveal that.

900
01:35:37,890 --> 01:35:40,270
We have to get out of this trouble first.

901
01:35:50,530 --> 01:35:52,000
Someone is coming.

902
01:35:56,150 --> 01:35:58,400
Go to your commanders, Rogatus.

903
01:36:10,310 --> 01:36:11,570
Do not move.

904
01:36:14,280 --> 01:36:15,150
Do not touch.

905
01:36:15,930 --> 01:36:17,640
There may be another trap.

906
01:36:34,480 --> 01:36:36,750
They noticed at the right time.

907
01:36:38,750 --> 01:36:40,330
They had time.

908
01:36:43,750 --> 01:36:44,820
Otherwise...

909
01:36:48,510 --> 01:36:49,820
Untie them.

910
01:36:50,420 --> 01:36:52,460
Untie them, let's see who they are.

911
01:37:15,770 --> 01:37:16,800
My Bey.

912
01:37:17,840 --> 01:37:20,320
These are the heroes
who saved us that day.

913
01:37:26,800 --> 01:37:29,080
They protected us earlier.

914
01:37:47,130 --> 01:37:48,130
My Bey.

915
01:37:55,680 --> 01:37:56,530
Boran.

916
01:38:05,240 --> 01:38:06,400
Boran.

917
01:38:12,950 --> 01:38:14,330
It's done, my Bey.

918
01:38:17,040 --> 01:38:17,880
My Bey.

919
01:38:20,280 --> 01:38:21,420
Brother!

920
01:38:28,350 --> 01:38:29,660
Are you fine?

921
01:38:30,220 --> 01:38:32,150
Thank Allah, my Bey.

922
01:38:40,840 --> 01:38:42,600
Brother.

923
01:39:16,350 --> 01:39:17,440
Konur?

924
01:39:40,260 --> 01:39:41,680
what are you doing here?

925
01:39:42,950 --> 01:39:45,130
Tell me why you came.

926
01:39:48,370 --> 01:39:50,600
I saw the truth, Osman Bey.

927
01:39:52,040 --> 01:39:54,080
What made you see...

928
01:39:56,080 --> 01:39:58,400
...the thing you didn't see earlier?

929
01:39:58,680 --> 01:40:00,400
Tell me.

930
01:40:04,820 --> 01:40:08,440
That Vizier tried to kill Hatuns.

931
01:40:10,820 --> 01:40:14,220
And you hid your face and
helped Hatuns.

932
01:40:15,460 --> 01:40:16,710
Right?

933
01:40:23,350 --> 01:40:25,570
I want to be with you from now on.

934
01:40:33,330 --> 01:40:34,510
Konur.

935
01:40:36,170 --> 01:40:41,080
We don't have hot food like Vizier offers,
neither a comfy bed.

936
01:40:43,080 --> 01:40:45,370
We don't have a place that offers food.

937
01:40:50,370 --> 01:40:54,820
Our food is here what
the shepherd gives us.

938
01:41:00,730 --> 01:41:02,640
A heart gains strength
as it faces hardships.

939
01:41:03,640 --> 01:41:05,440
It regresses as it faces easiness.

940
01:41:08,150 --> 01:41:10,000
I am with you, Osman Bey.

941
01:41:18,370 --> 01:41:20,800
The wound on my back is still there.

942
01:41:23,930 --> 01:41:25,750
What about yours?

943
01:41:27,620 --> 01:41:30,150
It may not heal the wound I caused, but...

944
01:41:33,530 --> 01:41:35,420
I brought you some important news.

945
01:41:41,220 --> 01:41:45,750
Geyhatu heard that Nicola
gathered the Lords.

946
01:41:49,110 --> 01:41:51,260
And he sent his soldiers to kill him.

947
01:41:55,440 --> 01:41:57,400
Why now?

948
01:42:01,680 --> 01:42:02,620
Why?

949
01:42:04,220 --> 01:42:06,060
I thought I was serving the truth

950
01:42:07,550 --> 01:42:09,550
I realised I was following falsehood.

951
01:42:14,110 --> 01:42:19,500
While I was saying that you are a rebel
I found out that I'm with the rebels.

952
01:42:23,420 --> 01:42:25,020
Tell me everything you know.

953
01:42:27,020 --> 01:42:29,200
It's hard to keep Geyhatu down.

954
01:42:29,770 --> 01:42:32,240
We made a mistake to invite him.

955
01:42:33,040 --> 01:42:37,150
It's like fire approaching to oil!

956
01:42:38,170 --> 01:42:40,820
He can burn down these lands.

957
01:42:41,820 --> 01:42:45,000
That's why you are in such a great power!

958
01:42:45,480 --> 01:42:48,400
Keep Geyhatu under your power.

959
01:42:49,370 --> 01:42:51,620
The destiny of these lands
is in your hands.

960
01:42:52,510 --> 01:42:54,970
Therefore, every solution is permitted.

961
01:42:56,130 --> 01:42:58,060
We can even agree with Pope...

962
01:42:58,640 --> 01:43:02,570
...if it comes to that point, Alem Shah.

963
01:43:03,060 --> 01:43:04,020
Keep that in mind.

964
01:43:04,840 --> 01:43:09,040
We will do what must be done.

965
01:43:15,130 --> 01:43:17,510
To ally with Pope, ha?

966
01:43:24,150 --> 01:43:25,550
Oh my God.

967
01:43:26,350 --> 01:43:28,680
Even I wasn't expecting all of this.

968
01:43:30,240 --> 01:43:31,660
Vizier surprised me.

969
01:43:32,220 --> 01:43:34,860
He's trying to do something
bigger than him.

970
01:43:36,310 --> 01:43:39,680
We can't even imagine Vizier's betrayals,
Kosses.

971
01:43:39,930 --> 01:43:43,150
To reach the top position...

972
01:43:43,530 --> 01:43:46,950
He can do everything, even risk
his life and everyone under him.

973
01:43:53,280 --> 01:43:55,000
Since when has he been meeting
that guy?

974
01:43:55,750 --> 01:43:57,000
They talked a few times.

975
01:43:57,930 --> 01:43:59,860
I only saw it once.

976
01:44:00,440 --> 01:44:05,200
Argun Khan sent 20 thousand soldiers
for Geyhatu.

977
01:44:06,750 --> 01:44:09,260
They want to take Turkish rebellion
under control.

978
01:44:09,840 --> 01:44:11,260
However...

979
01:44:12,000 --> 01:44:15,950
The goal of Geyhatu and Vizier
is to destroy us.

980
01:44:17,060 --> 01:44:20,620
Do you think Nikola knows that?

981
01:44:21,060 --> 01:44:22,930
Is this why he gathered the Lords?

982
01:44:22,930 --> 01:44:25,440
I don't think so.

983
01:44:26,130 --> 01:44:27,820
But he is doing the right thing.

984
01:44:37,350 --> 01:44:39,370
Now that you are on our side...

985
01:44:41,860 --> 01:44:43,060
...then...

986
01:44:45,460 --> 01:44:47,770
Stay with Vizier for a while.

987
01:44:51,420 --> 01:44:53,330
Bring me information from him.

988
01:44:56,550 --> 01:44:58,530
Information is everything.

989
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:01,510
Command is yours.

990
01:45:02,600 --> 01:45:03,510
My Bey.

991
01:45:18,530 --> 01:45:21,220
We'll take Nikola from Geyhatu's hand.

992
01:45:22,480 --> 01:45:26,000
- To kill him yourself, right Osman Bey?
- No.

993
01:45:27,660 --> 01:45:29,730
I need Nicola for now.

994
01:45:29,730 --> 01:45:32,270
How do you need him Osman Bey?
What are you saying?

995
01:45:33,060 --> 01:45:34,620
Let those dogs eat each other.

996
01:45:37,510 --> 01:45:39,970
We know what he did to Mari!

997
01:45:40,130 --> 01:45:42,280
Nikola!
We are talking about Nikola.

998
01:45:43,550 --> 01:45:47,730
My Bey, he is involved in every trouble
we face!

999
01:45:51,860 --> 01:45:53,260
Do it Osman Bey.

1000
01:46:02,000 --> 01:46:02,770
Do it.

1001
01:46:18,280 --> 01:46:20,040
When the dogs eat each other.

1002
01:46:21,710 --> 01:46:23,640
A stronger dog comes out of them.

1003
01:46:27,420 --> 01:46:31,710
Keep one by your side so that
you have the power to deal with the other.

1004
01:46:59,550 --> 01:47:01,020
I don't have a throne to sit on

1005
01:47:03,150 --> 01:47:05,400
There are not enough alps to win.

1006
01:47:06,970 --> 01:47:10,550
Enemies are like the sand on the desert!

1007
01:47:11,170 --> 01:47:12,550
That's why...

1008
01:47:14,860 --> 01:47:16,910
...To protect these lands...

1009
01:47:18,910 --> 01:47:20,910
I need Nicola.

1010
01:47:28,330 --> 01:47:31,970
Do not worry at all!

1011
01:47:33,750 --> 01:47:36,880
We will never forget what he did!

1012
01:47:37,640 --> 01:47:41,840
We will surely hold all the cruels
accountable!

1013
01:47:43,280 --> 01:47:47,660
And certainly when an innocent looks
back to see if there is anyone with them...

1014
01:47:48,750 --> 01:47:51,020
They will see us.

1015
01:47:56,950 --> 01:47:58,510
This is my last word.

1016
01:48:00,130 --> 01:48:01,200
Eyvallah.

1017
01:48:03,800 --> 01:48:05,310
Eyvallah.

1018
01:48:07,310 --> 01:48:08,640
Come on.

1019
01:48:16,120 --> 01:48:18,120
Sogut.

1020
01:48:18,120 --> 01:48:20,140
Can I come in, Vizier?

1021
01:48:21,820 --> 01:48:23,790
Enter.

1022
01:48:24,990 --> 01:48:29,020
Hadrat Vizier, you have a guest.
Do you allow him to enter?

1023
01:48:29,520 --> 01:48:30,520
Let him.

1024
01:48:40,320 --> 01:48:41,620
Welcome.

1025
01:48:42,020 --> 01:48:46,340
Sorry to hear what happened, Alam Shah.
I brought my Bey's blessings.

1026
01:48:46,820 --> 01:48:49,770
My Bey is very upset
about your health.

1027
01:48:50,540 --> 01:48:52,590
Thank him very much.

1028
01:48:52,840 --> 01:48:55,970
We are walking on the way of our
sacred case thanks to him.

1029
01:48:56,570 --> 01:48:58,820
We all are wounded for him.

1030
01:48:59,240 --> 01:49:02,090
We all suffer for his dreams.

1031
01:49:02,370 --> 01:49:03,440
Eyvallah. (thank you)

1032
01:49:03,970 --> 01:49:06,920
And we heard that Geyhatu
saved you by besieging the inn.

1033
01:49:17,270 --> 01:49:22,870
The punch of a relative is
better than the bread of a stranger.

1034
01:49:23,670 --> 01:49:26,320
I don't want the help
that will come from the Mongols.

1035
01:49:26,890 --> 01:49:30,920
Our intention is to save
this land from their oppression

1036
01:49:31,420 --> 01:49:35,640
We hope to expel
the Mongols and the infidels

1037
01:49:35,870 --> 01:49:38,320
And become the supreme state.

1038
01:49:38,820 --> 01:49:43,390
Just like when it was in the era of
Aladdin Keykubat

1039
01:49:44,420 --> 01:49:46,520
Osman is pursuing the same goal.

1040
01:49:47,570 --> 01:49:52,990
Osman Bey is very brave.

1041
01:49:54,090 --> 01:49:57,820
But he's a little guy.

1042
01:49:59,020 --> 01:50:04,120
What is his knowledge? Is he a statesman?
What is his educational attainment?

1043
01:50:05,420 --> 01:50:08,950
His grandfathers are shepherds,
and his ancestors are as well

1044
01:50:09,590 --> 01:50:11,770
He cannot create a state.

1045
01:50:12,090 --> 01:50:15,100
He is a Bey who takes care of sheep
and sleeps in a little tent

1046
01:50:15,170 --> 01:50:16,770
He shouldn't see too many dreams.

1047
01:50:17,040 --> 01:50:19,190
A land cannot have two leaders.

1048
01:50:19,370 --> 01:50:22,290
Kill him as soon as possible.

1049
01:50:25,020 --> 01:50:27,990
If only he knew when to obey.

1050
01:50:36,020 --> 01:50:39,640
I would make him a commander
of my army.

1051
01:50:43,040 --> 01:50:48,020
And now he's poor,
his head will be cut off

1052
01:50:53,370 --> 01:50:55,090
Son.

1053
01:50:57,240 --> 01:50:58,340
Dear Orhan.

1054
01:51:01,070 --> 01:51:09,070
May Allah let me see the days
that you ride horse and hold a sword!

1055
01:51:10,420 --> 01:51:11,640
Amin.

1056
01:51:13,640 --> 01:51:21,490
Be brave and always be on the side of
the truth and those with the truth.

1057
01:51:21,640 --> 01:51:23,990
- Amin.
- Amin.

1058
01:51:33,520 --> 01:51:40,190
Who knows, maybe you are thinking
why we are not in our tents.

1059
01:51:43,670 --> 01:51:46,630
I will warn you and your future brothers
and sister about....

1060
01:51:47,690 --> 01:51:51,490
....those munafiqs (fake believers)
like Vizier.

1061
01:51:54,990 --> 01:51:56,040
They...

1062
01:51:57,520 --> 01:52:03,490
They tried to set brothers against each other
in the past, and they do it now as well.

1063
01:52:06,990 --> 01:52:09,140
They won't stop in the future.

1064
01:52:11,690 --> 01:52:15,270
Their faces and names will change.

1065
01:52:16,140 --> 01:52:18,770
But their betrayal will not change.

1066
01:52:21,090 --> 01:52:22,820
Son.

1067
01:52:25,140 --> 01:52:28,540
There will always be enemies around you.

1068
01:52:33,090 --> 01:52:34,540
However...

1069
01:52:37,220 --> 01:52:42,540
As long as there are such
brave brothers by your side

1070
01:52:44,740 --> 01:52:47,240
No one will be able to defeat you!

1071
01:52:51,940 --> 01:52:57,090
And the great state
will advance on your shoulders!

1072
01:52:58,240 --> 01:52:59,720
Inshallah my Bey.

1073
01:53:10,890 --> 01:53:12,270
Alps!

1074
01:53:13,840 --> 01:53:15,790
Tomorrow is the time for war!

1075
01:53:16,840 --> 01:53:20,120
We will waste the hopes of the Vizier
and Geyhatu

1076
01:53:20,470 --> 01:53:22,490
- As you order my Bey.
- As you order, my Bey.

1077
01:53:47,640 --> 01:53:49,990
Say what you want to say, Geyhatu.

1078
01:54:24,370 --> 01:54:26,690
I'm here, Gündüz, I came.

1079
01:54:47,870 --> 01:54:49,390
Dear friends.

1080
01:54:50,190 --> 01:54:56,240
Geyhatu and the Vizier
want to wipe us off this land.

1081
01:54:58,470 --> 01:55:03,150
These men can't stand
anything about great Rome.

1082
01:55:03,150 --> 01:55:04,710
This is for sure.

1083
01:55:05,720 --> 01:55:11,690
Rogatus, Kosses.
Traitor Kosses.

1084
01:55:12,390 --> 01:55:15,390
They didn't deserve to be a Lord!

1085
01:55:15,640 --> 01:55:18,840
If they are not present
in the presidency of their castles...

1086
01:55:20,240 --> 01:55:23,090
...those castles are not anyone's, right?

1087
01:55:25,120 --> 01:55:26,370
Isn't that right?

1088
01:55:26,370 --> 01:55:32,240
I mean, we have to stand firm in front of
the Vizier and Geyhatu.

1089
01:55:32,820 --> 01:55:38,370
But, Nikola, I can't spoil
my relationship with Geyhatu for no reason.

1090
01:55:38,790 --> 01:55:41,290
I agree, both are very dangerous.

1091
01:55:41,290 --> 01:55:42,670
Real danger...

1092
01:55:43,090 --> 01:55:47,190
...is that they'll try to end us forever!
Can't you see that?

1093
01:55:50,790 --> 01:55:55,190
Today Harmankaya and Bilecik!
Tomorrow, Yarhisar! Inegol!

1094
01:55:55,570 --> 01:56:00,640
And all our lands one by one! If you don't
want to be erased from history forever...

1095
01:56:00,890 --> 01:56:03,870
We have only one chance!
We unite!

1096
01:56:04,090 --> 01:56:08,120
Our castle, our words!

1097
01:56:09,390 --> 01:56:15,840
We have to claim
Harmankaya and Bilecik again.

1098
01:56:16,290 --> 01:56:19,570
We owe this to great Rome, all of us!

1099
01:56:20,020 --> 01:56:22,720
- Aren't we?
- It's true what you're saying, Nicola.

1100
01:56:23,540 --> 01:56:24,720
You are right, Nicola.

1101
01:56:25,590 --> 01:56:26,720
So, Nikola...

1102
01:56:27,890 --> 01:56:31,390
How will this happen?
How will we get the castles back?

1103
01:56:35,540 --> 01:56:38,270
In the best way we know

1104
01:56:41,770 --> 01:56:43,490
By shedding their blood.

1105
01:56:44,840 --> 01:56:49,270
And if necessary, shed our blood

1106
01:56:49,690 --> 01:56:51,990
- Via war!
- Via bloodshed!

1107
01:56:51,990 --> 01:56:53,990
- Via war!
- For Rome!

1108
01:56:54,370 --> 01:56:55,390
For Jesus Christ!

1109
01:56:59,490 --> 01:57:01,040
That's it!

1110
01:57:01,890 --> 01:57:05,340
Standing up together!

1111
01:57:12,070 --> 01:57:14,570
Sir, Osman...

1112
01:57:15,700 --> 01:57:18,360
He escaped from
Geyhatu and Alam shah.

1113
01:57:25,710 --> 01:57:27,100
As you see...

1114
01:57:27,920 --> 01:57:29,240
There is Osman as well.

1115
01:57:30,780 --> 01:57:32,080
My dear friends.

1116
01:57:33,550 --> 01:57:38,760
Trouble never leaves this land.

1117
01:57:40,080 --> 01:57:41,880
We have only one solution

1118
01:57:43,110 --> 01:57:45,190
And that is to unite.

1119
01:57:51,180 --> 01:57:53,600
I'll go back to my castle
tomorrow morning.

1120
01:57:55,060 --> 01:57:58,410
And after I do all my preparations...

1121
01:57:59,980 --> 01:58:05,920
We're going out on the road to
Harmankaya from different places.

1122
01:58:08,000 --> 01:58:11,840
Why didn't we wait for
Alam Shah to recover before talking?

1123
01:58:12,560 --> 01:58:16,460
If we wait for that,
they will also heal their wounds.

1124
01:58:18,310 --> 01:58:21,730
The first one to stand up again
will win the war, Gündüz.

1125
01:58:24,360 --> 01:58:25,500
Nicola.

1126
01:58:27,110 --> 01:58:28,180
He'll die.

1127
01:58:30,960 --> 01:58:33,480
Inegol is ours now.

1128
01:58:33,850 --> 01:58:37,690
And then we'll take castles
of other Lords and their castles.

1129
01:58:38,220 --> 01:58:39,030
And then?

1130
01:58:40,130 --> 01:58:42,940
Is it our tribe's turn next, Geyhatu?

1131
01:58:45,760 --> 01:58:47,360
What can I take from your tribe?

1132
01:58:49,560 --> 01:58:51,100
No need to use force.

1133
01:58:51,460 --> 01:58:56,040
You will give me soldiers, horses
and supplies when I want.

1134
01:58:57,760 --> 01:59:00,470
Castles and fortresses will be yours.

1135
01:59:02,260 --> 01:59:05,900
You are the only ruler in
border areas, Gunduz.

1136
01:59:19,310 --> 01:59:20,380
Talk!

1137
01:59:21,090 --> 01:59:25,240
When we got out of the passage,
we were rained with arrows.

1138
01:59:25,930 --> 01:59:27,950
All soldiers died.

1139
01:59:29,530 --> 01:59:31,360
Why didn't you die?

1140
01:59:32,220 --> 01:59:34,280
Did Osman do this to you?

1141
01:59:36,910 --> 01:59:37,900
I couldn't see.

1142
01:59:38,440 --> 01:59:41,030
Where is Konur?
Where is Ferman?

1143
01:59:41,710 --> 01:59:42,760
They are dead.

1144
01:59:47,730 --> 01:59:49,220
Damn it!

1145
01:59:50,970 --> 01:59:52,010
Mingiyan.

1146
01:59:52,970 --> 01:59:54,540
Kill Nikola.

1147
01:59:56,170 --> 01:59:58,470
Never fail again.

1148
01:59:58,470 --> 02:00:00,120
By your order, Geyhatu.

1149
02:00:00,120 --> 02:00:01,100
Go!

1150
02:00:14,360 --> 02:00:16,570
How can you give
Orhan to Malhun Hatun, Ayse?

1151
02:00:16,970 --> 02:00:18,680
How can you let them go?

1152
02:00:20,520 --> 02:00:22,300
Sogut is boiling now!

1153
02:00:23,470 --> 02:00:25,650
How do you throw my nephew
in danger, Ayse?

1154
02:00:25,910 --> 02:00:30,110
Malhun Hatun is the mother of Orhan,
Gündüz, how was I supposed to say no?

1155
02:00:30,920 --> 02:00:33,900
Do you think that she doesn't care
her son as much as you do?

1156
02:00:33,950 --> 02:00:38,120
If she cared about her son, she wouldn't
question the order of Bey!

1157
02:00:38,610 --> 02:00:40,120
She wouldn't deserve exile!

1158
02:00:41,340 --> 02:00:43,060
Don't defend Malhun Hatun

1159
02:00:44,450 --> 02:00:47,340
What should I do?
Do I defend you against you?

1160
02:00:48,250 --> 02:00:49,780
Should I defend the Vizier?

1161
02:00:50,680 --> 02:00:54,250
They slander your brother,
you believe it, Gunduz!

1162
02:00:54,710 --> 02:00:56,250
Shall I tell you
well done?

1163
02:00:57,180 --> 02:00:59,340
Your mother and sisters are in danger!

1164
02:00:59,560 --> 02:01:02,220
You don't do anything
Do I give a pat you on the back?

1165
02:01:03,580 --> 02:01:06,020
The Mongols have entered Sogut,
Gündüz Bey!

1166
02:01:06,210 --> 02:01:09,310
You still listen to what Vizier says.

1167
02:01:10,430 --> 02:01:12,680
Should I tell you, well done?
What do you want me to tell you Gündüz?

1168
02:01:12,680 --> 02:01:13,960
Is enough

1169
02:01:15,690 --> 02:01:18,030
I don't want to hear even
a single word, Ayse.

1170
02:01:25,130 --> 02:01:25,870
Ayse.

1171
02:01:43,820 --> 02:01:48,190
I will burn the whole world down
for Orhan, Ayse.

1172
02:01:55,950 --> 02:01:56,960
Gunduz.

1173
02:01:59,510 --> 02:02:02,880
Have you ever seen a happy child
while being away from his mother?

1174
02:02:07,460 --> 02:02:10,350
Unless you cancel this exile...

1175
02:02:10,790 --> 02:02:15,050
Malhun Hatun will not
bring Orhan to the tribe.

1176
02:02:20,600 --> 02:02:22,010
I cancelled it already, Ayse.

1177
02:02:26,450 --> 02:02:27,760
I already did it.

1178
02:02:35,730 --> 02:02:37,680
I can't leave my nephew there, Ayse.

1179
02:02:42,550 --> 02:02:47,270
Also, if I can't protect my mother and
sisters while they are away from the tribe...

1180
02:02:49,550 --> 02:02:53,310
I shall have them with me.

1181
02:02:55,500 --> 02:03:00,490
I know they are not going to behave,
we'll conflict, but...

1182
02:03:02,530 --> 02:03:05,290
But I have to hit a happy medium.

1183
02:03:18,880 --> 02:03:20,950
I just want Orhan with us.

1184
02:03:23,290 --> 02:03:26,060
I just want my mother and sisters
to be safe.

1185
02:03:38,250 --> 02:03:40,100
I entrust you to Allah, my sheik.

1186
02:03:40,610 --> 02:03:44,730
If we don't go to the tribe now, we will
have betrayed the entrust of Osman Bey,

1187
02:03:46,060 --> 02:03:50,320
Taking care of the entrusts is
what you should do, my precious daughter.

1188
02:03:53,020 --> 02:03:57,160
Our return will be for the best,
even if it's Gunduz Bey's call, my sheik.

1189
02:03:59,040 --> 02:04:01,300
Thank Allah my mother is healthy again.

1190
02:04:01,730 --> 02:04:02,830
Thank Allah so much.

1191
02:04:03,290 --> 02:04:06,770
Gunduz Bey made a mistake.

1192
02:04:08,770 --> 02:04:12,230
He is now trying to make up
for that mistake.

1193
02:04:12,770 --> 02:04:17,230
Other than that,
Orhan will be safer in his tribe.

1194
02:04:22,750 --> 02:04:24,710
You are right, my Sheik, but...

1195
02:04:26,520 --> 02:04:30,560
I can't trust Gunduz Bey.
This may be a trap.

1196
02:04:31,730 --> 02:04:35,490
Only Allah can know the inside
of hearts, my beautiful daughter.

1197
02:04:36,570 --> 02:04:39,250
We will take measures just in case.

1198
02:04:39,830 --> 02:04:43,730
Let's hope Gunduz Bey's intention is pure.

1199
02:04:44,890 --> 02:04:46,123
Inshallah, my sheik.

1200
02:04:46,375 --> 02:04:47,390
Inshallah.

1201
02:04:48,170 --> 02:04:49,770
I entrust you to Allah.

1202
02:04:50,440 --> 02:04:51,410
I do as well.

1203
02:04:51,990 --> 02:04:53,860
I am grateful for what you did.

1204
02:04:56,970 --> 02:04:59,790
And you're one of
my daughters now, Mari.

1205
02:05:00,440 --> 02:05:02,240
I entrust you to Allah.

1206
02:05:02,700 --> 02:05:05,410
Sure, she's our daughter now.

1207
02:05:06,440 --> 02:05:10,310
She listened to us, married
a Turkish Bey.

1208
02:05:13,920 --> 02:05:16,260
May the other girls do the same as well.

1209
02:05:20,010 --> 02:05:20,990
Inshallah.

1210
02:05:23,660 --> 02:05:25,860
Let's go then,
my Sheik.

1211
02:05:26,810 --> 02:05:27,880
Go.

1212
02:05:28,410 --> 02:05:29,210
Mother.

1213
02:06:05,280 --> 02:06:09,480
Rogatus, our way seperates here.

1214
02:06:10,560 --> 02:06:12,310
Your way is to Iznik.

1215
02:06:13,280 --> 02:06:15,770
I will be waiting for you in Nikea,
Osman Bey.

1216
02:06:16,350 --> 02:06:19,790
I hope you save that stupid Nikola.

1217
02:06:23,060 --> 02:06:26,640
Eyvallah!
Your path shall be open!

1218
02:06:33,240 --> 02:06:35,840
Do not draw your weapon.

1219
02:06:36,010 --> 02:06:40,720
Otherwise, Mary will become a widow
And what do they call a brotherless woman?

1220
02:06:40,990 --> 02:06:44,040
- I will...
- Marie became my wife

1221
02:06:45,060 --> 02:06:46,790
Watch your movements.

1222
02:06:46,990 --> 02:06:51,810
I'll make you pay for
what you did to Mary.

1223
02:06:52,700 --> 02:06:53,700
Nicola.

1224
02:06:54,150 --> 02:06:58,660
Harmankaya is mine!

1225
02:07:03,610 --> 02:07:04,900
Come on!

1226
02:07:39,680 --> 02:07:41,240
Soldiers!

1227
02:07:44,970 --> 02:07:46,350
Attack!

1228
02:08:22,190 --> 02:08:26,460
I worked so hard to prevent this, but...

1229
02:08:28,460 --> 02:08:30,920
Because you followed Osman's stubbornness...

1230
02:08:32,350 --> 02:08:34,730
Many misfortunes have befallen us.

1231
02:08:39,810 --> 02:08:43,170
Thank Allah no one was hurt.

1232
02:08:44,990 --> 02:08:46,480
You are in the tribe now.

1233
02:08:47,170 --> 02:08:50,100
We are in the tribe to take care of our honesty
Gunduz Bey.

1234
02:08:50,610 --> 02:08:54,020
I won't bother myself
explaining your mistakes to you.

1235
02:08:54,860 --> 02:08:57,240
What's the point of explaining to
someone who doesn't understand?

1236
02:08:58,480 --> 02:09:00,190
He swore not to hear you.

1237
02:09:05,040 --> 02:09:06,660
You are right, Bala Hatun.

1238
02:09:08,040 --> 02:09:12,520
Nobody knows those people
better than me.

1239
02:09:16,520 --> 02:09:19,990
Keep that in mind!
You are my sisters...

1240
02:09:21,860 --> 02:09:23,900
You are my brother's entrust.

1241
02:09:25,520 --> 02:09:29,680
But whoever is trying to break up the tribe...

1242
02:09:30,900 --> 02:09:31,950
They should know that...

1243
02:09:33,660 --> 02:09:38,060
I will stand against them as long as I am
the Bey of this tribe

1244
02:09:42,150 --> 02:09:44,390
Whoever tries to divide the tribe...

1245
02:09:47,040 --> 02:09:49,080
I will punish them myself.

1246
02:10:08,500 --> 02:10:10,640
Boran, are you okay?

1247
02:10:11,350 --> 02:10:12,810
I'm fine my Bey!

1248
02:10:19,970 --> 02:10:22,350
Mongols on one side,
Turks on the other side!

1249
02:10:22,350 --> 02:10:23,660
Hell with you all!

1250
02:12:09,240 --> 02:12:10,120
Take him.

1251
02:12:20,190 --> 02:12:23,810
- Commander Geyhatu a messenger arrived.
- Let him come.

1252
02:12:27,720 --> 02:12:31,770
Arkun Khan...
Is it...

1253
02:12:57,900 --> 02:12:59,170
What is written, Geyhatu?

1254
02:13:01,610 --> 02:13:07,440
It says that a good deal of soldiers
are on their way to this land.

1255
02:13:08,460 --> 02:13:15,300
Argun Khan sent twenty thousand soldiers
under my command!

1256
02:13:16,680 --> 02:13:20,170
To put down the rebellion in the tribes!

1257
02:13:21,150 --> 02:13:22,210
I...

1258
02:13:23,350 --> 02:13:24,170
Vizier...

1259
02:13:27,500 --> 02:13:31,590
I will kill everyone!

1260
02:14:55,750 --> 02:14:57,120
Osman Bey!

1261
02:14:59,840 --> 02:15:02,040
Your effort to kill me...

1262
02:15:02,880 --> 02:15:04,370
...must be appreciated.

1263
02:15:04,700 --> 02:15:06,550
I will not give you to anyone

1264
02:15:08,550 --> 02:15:11,610
Your death will be at my hands

1265
02:15:12,970 --> 02:15:15,010
At my hands!

1266
02:15:43,950 --> 02:15:46,680
Death knocked on my door a lot of times,
Osman Bey.

1267
02:15:48,150 --> 02:15:50,320
But none of those attempts succeeded.

1268
02:15:50,680 --> 02:15:54,390
Don't trust your luck too much.

1269
02:17:52,718 --> 02:17:54,638
You will die

1270
02:17:55,680 --> 02:17:57,790
But...

1271
02:17:58,350 --> 02:18:00,840
I will kill you in such a way that...

1272
02:18:16,040 --> 02:18:17,058
But...

1273
02:18:18,840 --> 02:18:20,120
...not today

1274
02:18:32,610 --> 02:18:36,718
When you caught
a relentless enemy like me...

1275
02:18:38,920 --> 02:18:41,280
Won't you kill me?

1276
02:18:49,170 --> 02:18:50,520
Today...

1277
02:18:51,350 --> 02:18:54,480
...there is no friend or enemy.

1278
02:18:57,388 --> 02:19:03,010
We will move together to stay alive.

1279
02:19:04,110 --> 02:20:58,418
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com